# Status badges — always colorful

All **VCS / diff status badges** in the GUI must use the shared color map from `@/lib/vcsBadge`. Never gray `Badge variant="default"` / `variant="outline"` / `bg-primary` for file status.

## Single source of truth

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `sources/gui/frontend/src/lib/vcsBadge.ts` | `STATUS_BADGE_CLASS`, `vcsStatusBadgeClass()`, `diffStatusBadgeClass()` |
| `sources/gui/frontend/src/wails/forester.ts` | `vcsBadgeLabel()` — badge text (`A`, `M`, `D`, `N`) |
| `.cursor/interface/design-tokens.md` §3.5 | Spec reference |

## Color map (do not duplicate inline)

| Label | Meaning | Classes |
|-------|---------|---------|
| `A` | staged-new / Added | `bg-emerald-600 text-white` |
| `M` | modified (staged or unstaged) | `bg-amber-500 text-white` |
| `D` | deleted (staged or unstaged) | `bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground` |
| `N` | untracked | `bg-blue-600 text-white` |
| `R` | rename (History diff) | `bg-blue-600 text-white` when added |

## How to render

Use a plain `<span>` (or equivalent) with the helper class — **not** shadcn `Badge` for VCS status:

```tsx
import { vcsStatusBadgeClass } from "@/lib/vcsBadge";
import { vcsBadgeLabel } from "@/wails/forester";

<span
  className={cn(
    "flex h-[22px] min-w-[22px] items-center justify-center rounded-full px-1.5 text-xs font-semibold",
    vcsStatusBadgeClass(vcsStatus),
  )}
>
  {vcsBadgeLabel(vcsStatus)}
</span>
```

History changed files: `diffStatusBadgeClass(file.status)`.

## Do not

- Do **not** use `Badge variant="outline"` or `variant="default"` for VCS/diff status — outline resets colors; default is gray primary.
- Do **not** hardcode `bg-primary`, `bg-secondary`, `bg-muted`, or `text-muted-foreground` for status letters.
- Do **not** copy Tailwind color classes into components — extend `vcsBadge.ts` instead.
- Do **not** use Git-style `??` for untracked — label is **`N`**.

## Exceptions

- **Lock badge** (`lock` text) — intentionally `Badge variant="secondary"` / `bg-secondary`; not a VCS status.
- **Date / tag badges** on commit cards — secondary/default per commit-card spec.

## When adding a new status badge surface

1. Import helpers from `vcsBadge.ts` + `vcsBadgeLabel` if needed.
2. Render with `<span>` + shared classes.
3. Update `vcsBadge.ts` and `design-tokens.md` §3.5 if a new status code appears.

